# Generic solutions

Speech and decode code must work for any text the key can spell. Do not special-case a word, a phrase, or a test sentence in the implementation.

A word list or fixture loaded as data is fine. A branch that names a word is not.

```python
# Bad: the pangram is baked into the decoder
if heard == "coicl":
    return "quick"

# Good: the same rule applies to every word
if raw_word not in lexicon:
    return nearest_word(heard, lexicon)
```

Tests may quote example sentences. The code under test must not know which sentences those are.
